{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1521234-rose-themed-direlash-3ed","id":1521234,"title":"Rose-themed Direlash (3ed)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-22T22:52:59-07:00","id":1521234,"title":"Rose-themed Direlash (3ed)","content":"Hi everyone<br /> My group are talking about doing a 3ed Abyssal game (using the A Shadow Falls fanmade). I want to redo an old character, on fact the one of my avatar, Sinful Virtue. My problem is with the weapon; the character uses a (green jade?) Direlash based on a rose. Normally I don't care that much about a weapon being perfect for the character, but on this case the weapon is quite central to a character I am quite fond (even if honestly I didn't play it much on the old 2ed days).<br /> I have never created artifacts on 3ed. The numbers are really not a problem, but the evocations quite scare me. I want the weapon to have evocations based on blood, the thorns of a rose, and some others (possibly higher) based on the petals of the rose, but not really know how to proceed. Any help will be appreciated. I would like the artifact to be of 4 dots, but 5 dots if it is too powerful for 4 can be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12490-virtud","user":"Virtud","date":". 08-23-2023, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12490-virtud","name":"Virtud","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12490_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T10:41:39-07:00","id":1521264,"title":"","content":"Okay, don't worry too much about Evocations and instead focus on an innate power that feels true to previous versions of the character.<br /> What did it do in 2nd edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T14:20:10-07:00","id":1521282,"title":"","content":"Indeed, Evocations are like building an Exigent, except even easier because the one step at a time in which one takes it will only go for about six steps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T22:57:24-07:00","id":1521317,"title":"","content":"It was quite some years ago (my memory of the details is quite bad) and it was one of my first tries on 2ed, so not very balanced. It has two modes, the thorns one did extra damage on a grapple. The petals mode turned intangible and was impossible to parry. I would like to do something with a similar theme, but more appropiate for 3ed. Sadly, there are not many direlash to compare, at least that I can find on official material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12490-virtud","name":"Virtud","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12490_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T09:52:21-07:00","id":1521389,"title":"","content":"I can probably help you put something together. Did your direlash have a name? What dot rating are you wanting the updated version to have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T23:10:45-07:00","id":1521419,"title":"","content":"The name is Blood Rose Bramble (well, Zarzal de Rosa Sangre, the spanish version), and the idea is Artifact 4. The powers should go around the thorns, grapple, and a bit with sharp petals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12490-virtud","name":"Virtud","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12490_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-26T05:50:16-07:00","id":1521424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Virtud</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1521234-rose-themed-direlash-3ed?p=1521317#post1521317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was quite some years ago (my memory of the details is quite bad) and it was one of my first tries on 2ed, so not very balanced. It has two modes, the thorns one did extra damage on a grapple. The petals mode turned intangible and was impossible to parry. I would like to do something with a similar theme, but more appropiate for 3ed. Sadly, there are not many direlash to compare, at least that I can find on official material.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it\u2019s better to find wood jade and starmetal artifacts to compare for all the woody and immaterial effects in them o3o<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T14:50:14-07:00","id":1521536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Virtud</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1521234-rose-themed-direlash-3ed?p=1521419#post1521419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The name is Blood Rose Bramble (well, Zarzal de Rosa Sangre, the spanish version), and the idea is Artifact 4. The powers should go around the thorns, grapple, and a bit with sharp petals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we've got a lot to work with here. I'm picturing a whip made of braided forest-green leather, studded with tiny soulsteel thorns. The grip is carved ebony, with a pommel setting for a hearthstone and a bouquet of translucent glass roses ringing where the braided leather joins the grip. The lash is thirsty for living blood, drinking it in as it deals lethal damage to living creatures and turning the glass roses first pink and then crimson.<br /> <br /> The early Evocations focus on increasing decisive damage, hooking enemies with cruel thorns to drag them into a grapple, and maybe even on inflicting bleeding wounds that refuse to close. The later Evocations allow the user to spend the blood gained to do things like launch sprays of blood-red petal blades with a flick of the lash and animate the lash to twine around enemies. The capstone Evocation can only be used when the lash is fully gorged on blood and turns the glass roses a deep black-red as a garden of blood-red vines and black roses grows around the wielder.<br /> <br /> Does this sound like what you were aiming for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T16:03:22-07:00","id":1521550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1521234-rose-themed-direlash-3ed?p=1521424#post1521424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it\u2019s better to find wood jade and starmetal artifacts to compare for all the woody and immaterial effects in them o3o</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also advice worth considering. While each artifact is a unique wonder in-lore, sometimes what you want already exists in-print and if Ex3 homebrew isn't your forte (or you're making a moderately interesting artifact for an antagonist who might not survive contact with the PCs!) nothing breaks if you find evocations you like and copy them. Indeed, you'll probably get a better understanding of how things work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T12:07:36-07:00","id":1521609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1521234-rose-themed-direlash-3ed?p=1521536#post1521536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we've got a lot to work with here. I'm picturing a whip made of braided forest-green leather, studded with tiny soulsteel thorns. The grip is carved ebony, with a pommel setting for a hearthstone and a bouquet of translucent glass roses ringing where the braided leather joins the grip. The lash is thirsty for living blood, drinking it in as it deals lethal damage to living creatures and turning the glass roses first pink and then crimson.<br /> <br /> The early Evocations focus on increasing decisive damage, hooking enemies with cruel thorns to drag them into a grapple, and maybe even on inflicting bleeding wounds that refuse to close. The later Evocations allow the user to spend the blood gained to do things like launch sprays of blood-red petal blades with a flick of the lash and animate the lash to twine around enemies. The capstone Evocation can only be used when the lash is fully gorged on blood and turns the glass roses a deep black-red as a garden of blood-red vines and black roses grows around the wielder.<br /> <br /> Does this sound like what you were aiming for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I love that description. The bouquet and the colour-changing are new to the concept, but are now part of my headcanon. The rest is similar to what I was thinking. I am eager to see more of your ideas. Anyway, something with grapple is quite adecuate, but I really do NOT see the character using Brawl/Martial Arts. It would be much of a problem for the artifact to use the grapple with Melee instead?<br /> <br /> Usin other artifacts as a model was my original idea, but...which ones? the only plant based weapon I have seen is Burning Branch from Arms of the Chosen, and the fire is quite a different theme. There is Midnight Thorn, that concept is similar, but is an armor, not a weapon. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12490-virtud","user":"Virtud","date":". 08-29-2023, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12490-virtud","name":"Virtud","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12490_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T14:42:01-07:00","id":1521621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Virtud</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1521234-rose-themed-direlash-3ed?p=1521609#post1521609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Anyway, something with grapple is quite adecuate, but I really do NOT see the character using Brawl/Martial Arts. It would be much of a problem for the artifact to use the grapple with Melee instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought you said that the original artifact granted additional damage while grappling?<br /> <br /> Making grapple rolls with Melee instead of Martial Arts doesn't seem problematic directly, but it's not usually in theme for most artifacts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Usin other artifacts as a model was my original idea, but...which ones? the only plant based weapon I have seen is Burning Branch from Arms of the Chosen, and the fire is quite a different theme. There is Midnight Thorn, that concept is similar, but is an armor, not a weapon. </div> </div> </div>Lioness probably means that you go trolling through any artifact, not just the plant themed ones, and pull out Evocations that seem to do what you want mechanically. You can then dress them back up in rose fluff and have a workable artifact pretty fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T10:35:40-07:00","id":1521680,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1F8SlyPWqmkUZER7bsDZuj2Hfzqvz1p2YAQguf3nCGTI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's a first draft for the Evocations of the Bramble of Blood Roses</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}